# The Cessna 172P's control surfaces (src/gfx/parts.hpp says how a line is
# read): each a hinge line from its inboard or lower end to its other, in the
# model's body frame, metres from its origin - +x forward, +y starboard, +z
# down - then how far forward of the hinge the part reaches, how far aft, and
# how far either side of the hinge's plane; and first the JSBSim property
# whose value, in radians, is its deflection, with which way a positive value
# moves its trailing edge.
#
# Measured off the model's own sections (assets/models/c172p.mesh), by
# slicing it where each surface ends: the ailerons between 50% and 93% of the
# wing's semispan, each hinge a quarter of the local chord forward of the
# trailing edge;
# the elevators from 0.3 m out to 1.6 m, hinged three tenths of the
# chord forward of the trailing edge;
# the rudder from 0.6 m above the origin to 1.2 m,
# hinged three tenths of the chord forward of the trailing edge.
# The sections each was measured from are above its lines.
#
# wing -1.44..0.13 at 2.83 m, -1.09..0.04 at 5.26 m
surface left-aileron    fcs/left-aileron-pos-rad   down  -1.046 -2.830 -0.446  -0.808 -5.265 -0.530  0.000 0.470 0.189
surface right-aileron   fcs/right-aileron-pos-rad  down  -1.046 2.830 -0.446  -0.808 5.265 -0.530  0.000 0.470 0.189
# tail -5.51..-4.60 at 0.30 m, -5.33..-4.61 at 1.60 m
surface left-elevator   fcs/elevator-pos-rad       down  -5.236 -0.300 0.170  -5.111 -1.600 0.171  0.000 0.332 0.086
surface right-elevator  fcs/elevator-pos-rad       down  -5.236 0.300 0.170  -5.111 1.600 0.171  0.000 0.332 0.086
# fin -5.76..-4.77 at -0.60 m, -6.00..-5.35 at -1.25 m
surface rudder          fcs/rudder-pos-rad         right -5.464 -0.000 -0.600  -5.805 -0.000 -1.250  0.000 0.362 0.121
